1)Tag nginx it as mynginx:v1:                           docker tag nginx mynginx:v1
2)Tag it again as mynginx:latest:                       docker tag nginx mynginx:latest
3)List images and verify:                               docker images
4)Remove one tag and observe:                           docker rmi mynginx:v1
5)Observation:When you run this, Docker does not delete the image data (layers). Instead, it performs an "Untagged" operation. Because other tags (mynginx:latest and nginx:latest) still point to that Image ID, the image remains on your system. Docker only truly deletes the image layers when the last remaining tag is removed.

