Port mapping:
1) Run Nginx with Port Mapping:       docker run --name web-port-test -d -p 8080:80 nginx
2) Access in Browser:                 http://localhost:8080
3) List docker networks:              docker network ls
4)Inspect Default Bridge Network:     docker inspect network bridge
5) What Port Mapping DoesBy default, Docker containers are isolated and have their own private IP addresses that are not accessible from outside the host machine.Port mapping (-p host_port:container_port) acts as a "tunnel" or a bridge:The Request: When you visit localhost:8080, your computer sends a request to your Ubuntu OS on port 8080.The Translation: The Docker engine intercepts that traffic and forwards it to the container's internal port (port 80).The Response: The web server inside the container processes the request and sends the data back through the same tunnel to your browser.Without port mapping, your web application would be running "silently" inside the container, unreachable by any external users or browsers.
